# @title: .gitattributes — one line ending for the whole tree, and the files git must not touch.
# @state: text is LF in the index and in the working tree, on every machine.
# @dependencies: none stated.

# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS.
# The gates hash bytes, and a byte that differs by a line ending is a different byte.
# Four files had crept in with CRLF while the rest of the tree was LF, and a Windows checkout would have rewritten them again on every clone, which moves a pin that says nothing about the contract it protects.

# `text=auto` lets git detect text and store it with LF; `eol=lf` makes the working tree LF too, so a Windows editor cannot put CRLF back.

* text=auto eol=lf

# The files git must never touch: they are binary, and a line ending inside one changes what it is.

*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
*.crx binary
*.wav binary
*.mp3 binary
*.mp4 binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
